1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,177
A 2012 McKinsey report estimated that

2
00:00:02,177 --> 00:00:05,118
knowledge workers spend about twenty-eight percent

3
00:00:05,118 --> 00:00:07,119
of their workweek just reading and

4
00:00:07,119 --> 00:00:08,060
answering email.

5
00:00:08,060 --> 00:00:10,769
Programmers have a rule of three:

6
00:00:10,769 --> 00:00:13,725
the third time you repeat something,

7
00:00:13,725 --> 00:00:14,710
automate it.

8
00:00:14,710 --> 00:00:16,516
Apply it to your week.

9
00:00:16,516 --> 00:00:18,650
If you do the same digital

10
00:00:18,650 --> 00:00:20,046
task three times,

11
00:00:20,046 --> 00:00:21,770
stop and automate it.

12
00:00:21,770 --> 00:00:23,471
Start with three culprits:

13
00:00:23,471 --> 00:00:25,302
typing meeting action items,

14
00:00:25,302 --> 00:00:27,526
renaming email receipts for taxes,

15
00:00:27,526 --> 00:00:30,536
and reformatting one script into social posts.

16
00:00:30,536 --> 00:00:32,890
Modern AI workflows handle all three

17
00:00:32,890 --> 00:00:33,610
in seconds.

18
00:00:33,610 --> 00:00:36,391
Cut fifteen minutes of daily busywork

19
00:00:36,391 --> 00:00:38,871
and you get back about ninety-one

20
00:00:38,871 --> 00:00:40,900
hours a year for real work.

21
00:00:40,900 --> 00:00:43,080
Let software do the robot work

22
00:00:43,080 --> 00:00:45,187
so your brain stays sharp for

23
00:00:45,187 --> 00:00:46,640
high-value judgment.
